// "Holds off a fatal blow" -- no death-prevention/last-stand primitive
// exists anywhere in the engine (checked common/src/comp/buff.rs,
// common/src/states/). `Shielded` (a temp-HP absorb buff, already shipped
// on abjuration/shield.ron) is the closest existing approximation: enough
// of an HP buffer to plausibly "hold off" a blow that would otherwise
// land as the killing hit, though it doesn't truly guarantee survival the
// way the sheet's real death-ward mechanic does. Documented as an honest
// approximation, not the real mechanic.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    cast_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: Shielded, data: BuffData(strength: 60.0, duration: Some(60.0))),
    ],
    energy_cost: 75.0,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Abjuration),
        source: Some(Divine),
        // level 4 spell -> min_level 24, the level * 6 convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(24)),
    ),
)
